Roger Land writes (on digging out Gehannom): 
>Actually, it didn't take nearly as long as you might think.  I did most
>of the excavation polymorphed into an Umber Hulk (seems much faster than
>using a pickaxe).  Having a PYEC ensured ample charges for my wands of
>polymorph and light.  I was also assisted by the game itself.  I was
>followed virtually the entire trip through hell by 2 or 3 peaceful
>Umber Hulks.  They kept falling through trap doors to the next level
>down.  Didn't even need to tame them.

Pet umber hulks are awesome.  Unfortunately, I'm pretty sure they 
don't lay eggs.  I'm still far too lazy to tunnel out a level that
way (at about four moves per square, I think), but it's fun to 
leave tame or peaceful umber hulks all over the place and let them 
unmaze the mazes while you go play the game.  It's not like cleaning
out all the walls for the true NetHack claustrophobe, but it makes
getting around really simple anyway.  

It's tough to do this kind of thing without a PYEC, though, and I've
given up wishing for quest artifacts as part of my quest for purity.
Time to go for the Tourist ascension, I guess.

